  "title": "Coast Guard medevacs cruise ship passenger 15 miles east of Charleston",
  "description": "CHARLESTON, S.C. — Coast Guard crews medevaced a 46-year-old woman Tuesday from the cruise ship Carnival Pride 15 miles east of Charleston. \r\n\r\nThe woman was reported to have suffered a stroke.\r\n\r\nCoast Guard Sector Charleston watchstanders received notification at 6:27 p.m. Monday and launched a Coast Guard Air Station Savannah MH-65 Dolphin rescue helicopter crew at 7 a.m. due to low visibility from heavy fog Monday night.\r\n\r\nThe woman and a nurse were hoisted and taken to Roper St. Francis Hospital at 8:13 a.m.\r\n\r\nThe woman was reported to be in stable condition.",
